WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.141 --> 00:00:01.787
- [Kelly] You look so nice.

00:00:01.787 --> 00:00:03.229
I love this outfit!

00:00:03.229 --> 00:00:04.229
- I appreciate it.

00:00:04.229 --> 00:00:05.815
- [Kelly] Is it green?

00:00:05.815 --> 00:00:06.648
- Yes. Yes.

00:00:06.648 --> 00:00:07.481
- [Kelly] I dunno what that is.

00:00:07.481 --> 00:00:08.314
I love it.

00:00:08.314 --> 00:00:09.570
- It's greenish.
- Greenish. Okay.

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:10.930
Am I color-blind? Is it not green?

00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:12.575
- I mean...

00:00:12.575 --> 00:00:13.575
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:13.575 --> 00:00:14.408
- Greenish.

00:00:14.408 --> 00:00:15.241
- What's that?

00:00:15.241 --> 00:00:16.200
- Well, I have to tell you, see?

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.080
Well, I come bearing a gift.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:18.913
- [Kelly] You're my favorite guest.

00:00:18.913 --> 00:00:20.890
- Yes. Here's the thing.

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:23.220
My wife, Jazmyn Simon,
wrote a children's book.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:24.053
- [Kelly] Oh, yeah.

00:00:24.053 --> 00:00:25.600
- It's called "The Most Perfect You".

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:26.433
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:00:26.433 --> 00:00:28.340
- It's an ode to motherhood and self-love.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:29.173
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:00:29.173 --> 00:00:30.100
- And it's a reminder to anyone

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.200
who's ever compared themself to anyone,

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.504
that they're perfect exactly
the way that they are.

00:00:34.504 --> 00:00:35.580
(audience applauds)

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:38.702
- I hope the book's in there for my kid.

00:00:38.702 --> 00:00:40.424
- [Dule] See, in honor of Rad Moms Week,

00:00:40.424 --> 00:00:43.000
one rad mom, my wife, Jazmyn Simon,

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.440
wanted to present to you, another rad mom,

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:47.500
this token of love to remind you

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:49.160
that you are and always will be

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:49.993
the most perfect you.

00:00:49.993 --> 00:00:51.660
- I love this!

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.540
We read every night.

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:55.373
- [Dule] It's a great book.

00:00:55.373 --> 00:00:56.810
- Literally, my kids, we read every night,

00:00:56.810 --> 00:00:57.850
and my daughter loves it.

00:00:57.850 --> 00:00:59.890
And she loves the ones
where she feels represented.

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:01.820
Like it's a girl, it's about
a girl, she loves that.

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:02.990
- It's a beautiful story.

00:01:02.990 --> 00:01:04.750
So I really hope they enjoy it.

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:05.734
- This is awesome.

00:01:05.734 --> 00:01:07.570
What a cool thing to do.

00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:09.320
So how old are your kids?

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:10.830
- Well, we have a 17-year-old.

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:11.663
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:01:11.663 --> 00:01:12.496
- Yes.
- [Kelly] Oh,

00:01:12.496 --> 00:01:13.810
you gotta stretch.
- Named Kennedy Irie,

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:15.550
who is off to Northwestern next year.

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:16.450
- [Kelly] Oh, yeah? Congratulations.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:17.340
- [Dule] So very proud of her.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:20.590
And we have a two-year-old named Levi,

00:01:20.590 --> 00:01:21.878
who is running the show.

00:01:21.878 --> 00:01:23.510
He runs the show.

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:25.700
- Oh my gosh. Levi. Those cheeks?

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:26.640
- He's such such a joy.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:27.473
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:27.473 --> 00:01:28.700
I know the baby smell, all of it.

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:29.660
I had a puppy on me earlier

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:30.790
and I'm still smelling it.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:31.623
- [Dule] Oh, man.

00:01:31.623 --> 00:01:32.456
- Do y'all have animals?

00:01:32.456 --> 00:01:33.560
- He actually wanted to come today.

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.547
I said, "Dada's gonna do an interview."

00:01:35.547 --> 00:01:36.720
"I wanna come do an interview."

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:37.760
- [Kelly] I love that.

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:39.170
- But Mama, you can come, too.

00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:40.768
- Bring them! Next time.

00:01:40.768 --> 00:01:41.910
It's a family event,

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:43.250
I'm just saying.

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:44.930
So wait, we were just talking
about first ladies, though.

00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:46.790
And I know everybody knows
you were on "West Wing", right?

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:47.890
So did you ever,

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:49.568
you had to have at some point,

00:01:49.568 --> 00:01:52.800
just like taken a tour, at
least, of the West Wing.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.250
And if you didn't, what a travesty.

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:55.083
- [Dule] I did.

00:01:55.083 --> 00:01:56.910
I got a chance to go there a few times.

00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:57.890
First, I was able to go there

00:01:57.890 --> 00:01:59.497
during the Clinton administration

00:01:59.497 --> 00:02:00.590
a couple times.

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:03.140
And I was able to go there
during the Obama administration

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:04.590
and during the Bush administration.

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:05.423
- Wow.

00:02:05.423 --> 00:02:06.440
- Yeah, it was, I know the place.

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:07.390
- You were checking all those boxes.

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:09.149
- [Dule] I know the place pretty well.

00:02:09.149 --> 00:02:09.982
- Yeah.
- [Dule] Pretty well.

00:02:09.982 --> 00:02:10.815
- Okay.

00:02:10.815 --> 00:02:11.970
So what was the coolest thing
you ever got to do there?

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:12.870
- [Dule] Well, I will say

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:15.350
the coolest coolest thing
that I ever got a chance to do

00:02:15.350 --> 00:02:17.480
was to bring my grandmother
to the Oval Office.

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:18.313
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:02:18.313 --> 00:02:19.146
- That was pretty surreal

00:02:19.146 --> 00:02:20.235
because my family's from Jamaica.

00:02:20.235 --> 00:02:22.387
So she emigrated and then to see

00:02:22.387 --> 00:02:25.890
her grandchild now be able to
bring her to the Oval Office.

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:26.723
- [Kelly] That's is pretty cool.

00:02:26.723 --> 00:02:28.520
- She said, "Look what I lived to see.

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:30.070
Look what I lived to see."

00:02:30.070 --> 00:02:30.970
- [Kelly] Oh, wow.

00:02:30.970 --> 00:02:32.280
(audience cheers)

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:33.449
That's powerful.

00:02:33.449 --> 00:02:35.210
- [Dule] The second coolest thing

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:36.610
that I got a chance to do

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:39.737
was to tap dance on the
roof of the White House.

00:02:39.737 --> 00:02:40.609
- [Kelly] What?!

00:02:40.609 --> 00:02:41.442
- [Dule] Yeah.

00:02:41.442 --> 00:02:42.275
I got a chance.

00:02:42.275 --> 00:02:43.130
- [Kelly] How did you swing that?

00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:44.015
- [Dule] Well, one, I'm a tap dancer.

00:02:44.015 --> 00:02:45.230
- [Kelly] Well, no, I know that part,

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:46.063
you're a dancer.

00:02:46.063 --> 00:02:47.540
But they just let people up on the roof?

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:49.297
They never let me, and I've
been there several times.

00:02:49.297 --> 00:02:51.700
- I was giving a tour around the place

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:54.050
and I ended up being in this room,

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:58.020
and it was between the
residence and the West Wing.

00:02:58.020 --> 00:02:59.340
Or the residence and the East Wing,

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:01.729
there's like a portico.

00:03:01.729 --> 00:03:03.680
There's a window going out there.

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:04.513
And I said,

00:03:04.513 --> 00:03:06.360
"Is it okay if I just
go out there and dance?

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:07.760
I mean, if I can,"

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:08.780
and they said, "Sure."

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:10.450
I went out there and I tap-danced

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:11.860
and there you go.

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:12.693
- [Kelly] Oh my God.

00:03:12.693 --> 00:03:13.526
- Then on top of that,

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:15.650
I was able to dance out in
the Press Briefing Room.

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:16.617
- [Kelly] I love it, you're like,

00:03:16.617 --> 00:03:17.560
"I'm gonna dance all over."

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:18.500
- [Dule] Oh, yeah. I'm gonna dance over.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:21.830
In that shot, I also paid
homage to Gregory Hines,

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:23.080
'cause there's a step in there that I did

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:25.060
that is always Gregory Hines' step

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:25.893
and I gotta do it here.

00:03:25.893 --> 00:03:26.870
- Okay. What's the one move?

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:27.703
I don't know.

00:03:27.703 --> 00:03:29.660
- I'll show you.

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:30.640
- Oh, you did the turn!

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:31.473
Okay.

00:03:31.473 --> 00:03:32.555
- You see what I'm saying?

00:03:32.555 --> 00:03:34.320
(audience cheers)

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:35.153
- I love Gregory.

00:03:35.153 --> 00:03:36.130
I always gotta big up Gregory

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:37.454
every time I have a chance to do it.

00:03:37.454 --> 00:03:38.287
You know what I mean?

00:03:38.287 --> 00:03:39.120
- I love that.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:39.990
I just love that you love dancing so much.

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:41.110
It feels so good.

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:41.950
- Right.

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:42.850
- So wait, you're now doing

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:43.851
the remake of "The Wonder Years".

00:03:43.851 --> 00:03:44.684
- [Dule] Yes.

00:03:44.684 --> 00:03:45.830
- So did you, were you
a fan of the original?

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:47.110
- [Dule] I was a fan of the original.

00:03:47.110 --> 00:03:47.943
I really enjoyed it.

00:03:47.943 --> 00:03:49.120
You couldn't be a child of the '80s

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:51.360
and not be a fan of the original show.

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:53.330
Who didn't have a crush on Winnie Cooper?

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:55.600
- [Kelly] I never
stopped hearing her name.

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:58.330
- But I did also realize at that time

00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:00.529
that I did not see myself
reflected in the show.

00:04:00.529 --> 00:04:02.441
As much as I love this show

00:04:02.441 --> 00:04:03.274
and appreciate this show,

00:04:03.274 --> 00:04:04.510
I didn't see myself.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.000
Even as we were talking
about with the book,

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.290
representation matters.

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:08.200
- [Kelly] Absolutely.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:09.150
It's empowering.

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:10.320
So when the opportunity came up for me

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:11.740
to do this show,

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:13.000
I wanted to jump at it.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:14.160
I knew that Saladin Patterson

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:15.170
was the creator of the show,

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:16.793
who I'd known for years.

00:04:16.793 --> 00:04:19.320
He's a dynamic writer.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.303
And then when I knew that EJ Williams

00:04:21.303 --> 00:04:22.153
was gonna be a part of it,

00:04:22.153 --> 00:04:25.260
and Saycon Sengbloh and Laura Kariuki,

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:26.093
I just thought it was important

00:04:26.093 --> 00:04:28.067
to be able to expand the lens.

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:29.673
"The Wonder Years" belongs to all of us.

00:04:29.673 --> 00:04:30.985
"The Wonder Years" is not just

00:04:30.985 --> 00:04:32.810
from one group of people.

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:34.900
This is one story of "The Wonder Years".

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:36.140
I think the show can be re-imagined

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:36.973
in many different ways.

00:04:36.973 --> 00:04:37.806
- Absolutely.

00:04:37.806 --> 00:04:40.610
- [Dule] You know, America
is a great melting pot,

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:42.680
and I think if we can show that more,

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:44.330
it can also help bridge gaps

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:45.850
and unify people and
bring people together,

00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:46.923
and that's one reason I
want to be part of that.

00:04:46.923 --> 00:04:48.723
(audience applauds)
- [Kelly] 100%.

